@SYSTEM_TITLE
; GETKEY / GETKEYTRIGGERED / MOUSEX / MOUSEY / ISACTIVE with no window,
; which is exactly the state Emuera itself is in before `MainWindow` exists:
; `GetMousePosition` returns `new Point()` (`GameView/EmueraConsole.cs:1983-1984`)
; and no key can be down. `ISACTIVE` is `EmueraConsole.IsActive`, which this
; fork defines as `return true` (`:276-277`).

; 0x10 is VK_SHIFT — the key eraMegaten polls most often.
PRINTFORML GETKEY(VK_SHIFT) = {GETKEY(0x10)}
; `keycode < 0 || keycode > 255` returns 0 before touching the toggle latch
; (`GameData/Function/Creator.Method.cs:6722-6723`).
PRINTFORML GETKEY(-1) = {GETKEY(-1)}
PRINTFORML GETKEY(256) = {GETKEY(256)}
; The latch says "newly pressed", but the key is not down, so the AND fails
; (`:6732`).
PRINTFORML GETKEYTRIGGERED(VK_SHIFT) = {GETKEYTRIGGERED(0x10)}
; A second query in the same run: still 0, and still for the down bit.
PRINTFORML GETKEYTRIGGERED(VK_SHIFT) = {GETKEYTRIGGERED(0x10)}
PRINTFORML MOUSEX() = {MOUSEX()}
PRINTFORML MOUSEY() = {MOUSEY()}
PRINTFORML ISACTIVE() = {ISACTIVE()}
